    "Slope": {
        "name": "Slope",
        "description": "Slope sends a rolling ball racing down a glowing neon track and asks how long you can keep it alive. The course is a narrow ribbon of platforms broken up by gaps, sharp turns, and red blocks, and the ball keeps picking up speed the longer you survive. Each stretch leaves a little less time to react than the last, so the real challenge is staying calm while the pace climbs.\n\nSteer with the left and right arrow keys or A and D, and click the game area first so it registers your keys. Short taps usually work better than holding a direction, because a long press can carry you straight off the edge. Look ahead rather than at the ball: the next turn or obstacle is what you need to be lining up for, and early, gentle corrections leave room to fix mistakes.\n\nUse your first few runs to get a feel for how quickly the ball responds, then aim to beat your own best distance rather than reaching any particular point. Every fall is over in seconds, so retrying is quick, and each attempt teaches a little more about reading the track early. That fast loop is what makes Slope easy to pick up and hard to put down.",
        "metaDescription": "Play Slope free in your browser. Steer a fast ball down a neon track, dodge obstacles, handle sharp turns, and avoid the gaps.",
        "url": "games/Slope-Game-main/index.html",
        "image": "thumbnails/slope.jpg",
        "tags": ["racing", "action", "difficult", "favorite"]
    },
