    "TheImpossibleQuiz": {
        "name": "The Impossible Quiz",
        "description": "The Impossible Quiz lives up to its name by turning ordinary quiz questions into traps. The obvious answer is rarely right, some questions are not really about what they ask, and a few reward actions that have nothing to do with the question text. Your lives are limited, so each wrong guess costs you something you cannot easily get back.\n\nMost questions are answered with the mouse, though some expect something unexpected, so look at the whole screen before committing. Read the wording closely, check the background and any moving elements, and ask yourself whether a question might be a joke before overthinking it. When a question seems to have no sensible answer, try interacting with things you would not normally click.\n\nTreat each failed run as research. The questions come in a fixed order, so what you learn about the early ones carries over to your next attempt. The game works best with patience and a sense of humor: you are meant to be fooled, and getting past a question that fooled you is the reward.",
        "metaDescription": "Play The Impossible Quiz and tackle tricky questions, unexpected answers, and logic that rarely follows the obvious route.",
        "url": "games/html/quiz.html",
        "image": "thumbnails/impossiblequiz.png",
        "tags": ["puzzle", "strategy", "difficult", "adventure", "favorite"]
    },
